// GM Battle Manager — a single-user combat tracker for running D&D and friends.
// Initiative order, hit points, conditions and effects — no board, no
// multiplayer, no walls, no fog of war, no chat. The DM runs the whole fight
// alone. The tracker auto-saves to this browser (localStorage) and resumes
// on reload.

$meta
  title = GM Battle Manager
  description = A single-user GM combat tracker for D&D — add heroes, monsters and NPCs to an initiative list, track hit points with quick damage/heal buttons, and apply conditions and effects. No accounts, no multiplayer: the DM runs the whole table alone and it auto-saves in the browser.
  tags = tabletop, rpg, dnd, battle manager, virtual tabletop, gm tool, initiative tracker
  image = https://user.uploads.dev/file/786af8ab520759d100a14af5b32fba04.jpg

hubUrl = https://perchance.org/bgn-boardgame-network
gameTitle = GM Battle Manager
gameTagline = Your combat tracker for D&D and friends. Drop heroes, monsters and NPCs into the initiative order, track hit points, apply conditions, and roll the dice as the DM.
gameKicker = Initiative · HP · Conditions · Effects
gameGenre = GM Battle Tool
gamePlayers = 1 GM
accentColor = #d4af37
heroImage = https://user.uploads.dev/file/786af8ab520759d100a14af5b32fba04.jpg

createServerSocket = {import:server-plugin}

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// PLANNED FEATURES — the GM Battle Manager roadmap, mapped 1:1 from the
// feature surface of the Foundry VTT dnd5e system (github.com/foundryvtt/dnd5e).
// Already shipped: the initiative tracker with round counter, hit point
// tracking with damage/heal, effects and status conditions, the DM dice
// roller, the full combat engine (attacks vs AC, crits, damage formulas with
// type modifiers, saves and checks, concentration with auto CON saves,
// automatic death saves, combatant groups), the DM stat sheet (ability scores
// auto-deriving saves and checks, save/skill proficiency, hit dice, condition
// immunities, languages) and auto-save. Everything below is on the roadmap.
//
// REFERENCE: the dnd5e system source is at https://github.com/foundryvtt/dnd5e
// — use it (module/, templates/, data/ + packs/_source/) to check how each
// feature is implemented upstream before building it here.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
plannedFeatures
  intro = Roadmap for the GM Battle Manager, modeled on the feature surface of the Foundry VTT dnd5e game system and trimmed to what makes sense for a single-user DM initiative tracker — no battle board, no player character sheets, no inventory management, no chat, no player-facing tools. Items already in the table today are marked SHIPPED.

  actors
    label = Actor Sheets (DM-facing stat blocks)
    features
      npc sheet with auto-calculated challenge rating and experience award
      monster sheet with legendary actions, lair actions and regional effects
      vehicle sheet with crew and stations
      group sheet for running many monsters as one encounter
      ability scores - strength, dexterity, constitution, intelligence, wisdom, charisma - SHIPPED: each combatant's manager holds six ability scores (1-30) that auto-derive every dependent number
      ability modifiers and saving throws, auto-derived from scores and effects - SHIPPED: modifiers are computed from scores, save proficiency toggles add the proficiency bonus, and active effects stack on top; every save and check rolls these live
      all 18 skills with proficiency, expertise, half and double proficiency - SHIPPED: click a skill chip to cycle proficient ✧ / expertise ✧✧ / half ½; bonus = ability modifier + level × proficiency bonus + effects
      hit points, hit dice and death saving throws with automatic rolls - SHIPPED: HP tracked on the row, hit dice (e.g. 5d8) roll and heal from the combatant's manager, and automatic death saves trigger at 0 HP
      armor class with formula-driven calculation from equipment and effects
      movement speeds - walk, fly, swim, burrow, climb and hover
      senses - darkvision, blindsight, tremorsense and truesight
      damage vulnerabilities, resistances and immunities - SHIPPED
      condition immunities and special traits - SHIPPED: condition immunities are listed on the combatant sheet (special traits are modeled as custom effects)
      languages plus tool, armor and weapon proficiencies - SHIPPED: languages are listed on the combatant sheet (tool/armor/weapon proficiencies remain a free-text field on the roadmap)
      initiative derived from dexterity plus class features and effects

  combat
    label = Combat and Dice
    features
      DM dice roller - SHIPPED: roll d20/d12/d10/d8/d6/d4 (and damage dice) with a flat modifier, advantage/disadvantage and a dice count; every roll logs its dice and total in a log and can apply the total as damage or healing straight to any combatant's hit points
      attack rolls with auto-modifiers, damage rolls and critical hits - SHIPPED: pick an actor and target and roll d20 + the attacker's Attack bonus against the target's AC; natural 20 always hits and doubles the damage dice, natural 1 always misses, and a hit offers an auto damage roll from the attacker's stored damage formula
      damage formulas with multiple types and spell-level scaling - SHIPPED: damage formulas like 2d6+1d4+3 are parsed for attacks and the dice tray; damage type is chosen at apply time and checked against each combatant's immunities, resistances and vulnerabilities
      saving throws with auto-applied proficiency - SHIPPED: six save modifiers per combatant (auto-derived from your stats, plus effects); the Save action rolls d20 + modifier and auto-applies concentration CON saves with the right DC when damaged
      ability checks and skill checks with modifier dialogs - SHIPPED: the Check action rolls d20 + the combatant's ability/skill modifier plus effects plus an on-the-fly bonus
      initiative tracker with sorting and turn advancement - SHIPPED
      conditions - blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, stunned, unconscious and more - SHIPPED (status conditions with rules-backed modifier bundles)
      concentration tracking with automatic saving throws on damage - SHIPPED: set a spell on the combatant's combat stats; any damage rolls an automatic CON save (DC 10 or half damage, whichever is higher) and drops concentration on failure
      automatic death saves when a token drops to zero hit points - SHIPPED: at 0 HP the tracker row gains a death-save button (and the manager shows fail/success pips); natural 20 regains 1 HP, natural 1 is two fails, three fails kills, three successes stabilizes, and extra damage while down counts as a failure
      damage and healing application with type modifiers - SHIPPED: damage rolls and quick buttons apply type modifiers - immune deals none, resistant halves, vulnerable doubles - with the applied amount and reason logged
      encounter sheets for grouping monsters - SHIPPED: save the whole table as a named encounter (combat stats, groups and damage types included) and drop it back into any fight
      combatant groups inside the tracker - SHIPPED: give combatants a group name (e.g. "Goblins") in their combat stats and the tracker groups them under a collapsible shared header
      hit points and hit dice tracked on the combatant itself - SHIPPED (quick damage/heal buttons on each tracker row, HP/max shown in the tracker, exact HP plus drop-to-0 and heal-to-full in the combatant manager)

  effects
    label = Active Effects
    features
      active effects granting bonuses to abilities, skills, saves and attacks - SHIPPED: add/remove effects on any combatant by clicking its tracker row; stored per combatant, shown as colored dots and a detail list in the combatant manager; source attribution recorded
      effect durations with automatic expiry - SHIPPED: set a duration in rounds when applying an effect; a Round counter in the Initiative panel advances when Next ▶ cycles past the last combatant, and round-limited effects auto-expire when their rounds elapse
      applied effects tied to status conditions - SHIPPED: one-click standard conditions (Blinded, Charmed, Poisoned, Restrained, ...) in the combatant manager; each applies its rules-backed modifier bundle (flat −2 ≈ disadvantage) and shows a colored status dot on the tracker row; conditions without modifiers are status markers only — hard rules (auto-failed saves, movement locks, no actions, crits) intentionally excluded until the combat engine lands
      source attribution showing where each bonus comes from
      effect tooltips on tokens

  ui
    label = Sheets and Tools
    features
      full npc, vehicle and group sheets
      roll dialogs with modifiers and configuration
      macros for reusing common actions
      journal with note, class and rule pages
      compendium browser to search and filter content - monsters, items, spells and more - SHIPPED: a searchable library of ~24 SRD monsters (search by name/type/trait, filter by creature type) that drops full stat blocks — AC, attacks, ability scores, saves, skills, damage types, languages — into the tracker with one tap
      property attribution for every derived number
      tooltips throughout the interface
      calendar support with setting calendars
      settings panel for homebrew configuration
